	'register' => 'The whole site is formal Mainland business Simplified Chinese and addresses the reader as 您, in every string and every slot — body copy, headings, eyebrows, ALL-CAPS bands, buttons, form labels, placeholders, alt and aria text, the <title>, the meta description, og: tags and JSON-LD. Never write 你／你的／你们 anywhere, and never invent the non-existent plural honorific 您们 — several readers are still 您. Company voice is 我们 (本公司 only in contracts and legal notices), never 咱们. BUTTONS AND LINK LABELS follow native Chinese web-UI convention: keep the verb of the English and write a short verb-object phrase with no pronoun and no final 。 — "Browse catalog" is 浏览产品目录, "Request a demo" is 申请演示, "Download" is 下载, "Contact us" is 联系我们. Never flatten a verb label into a bare noun (产品目录, 下载中心 are wrong for those) and never leave a Chinese verb without its object (下载聊天记录, not 下载聊天). The honorific 垂询 is company-voice invitation wording only (欢迎垂询) and must NEVER appear on a clickable label, tab, option value or form heading — every "... sales inquiry" label is 销售咨询. Everything that is not a control label — prose, headings, questions, metadata — addresses the reader as 您.',
