	'nuances' => array(
        'INDUSTRY STYLE (native technical editor): Claims: say only what the English proves. No 最/第一/顶尖/卓越/革命性 unless the source has it; industry-leading = 行业领先, never 业界第一. Headings and CTAs are short verb-object phrases with no 。 or ！ (申请报价, 获取报价, 咨询专家, 下载宣传册). Spec labels are nouns (整机质量, 外形尺寸); table values are 是/否/选配/标配. Units: keep the source unit and figure exactly — an imperial figure keeps ″ (18″ × 30″, never 18 英寸) and gains no conversion (never （457 × 762 mm）). Write SI symbols after a half-width space (16 kg, 200 L/min, 29 bar, 10 N·m, g·mm), never 千克/巴/升/克·毫米. Use decimal points (0.75), en-dash ranges (40–420 mm), and 7×24 小时 for 24/7. Undo English syntax: put the condition first (如需…，请…), drop filler 它/进行/能够 but keep an ownership 我们的／旗下 (our many brands = 旗下众多品牌), avoid 被 passives and 通过……从而…… chains, and use no more than two 的 per noun phrase. Half-width / only inside Latin or number runs (12V/24V); brand and model names in source case (DATAMES, Winbal); Image 1 → 图 1. One term per concept: 动平衡机 (not 平衡机), 试验台 (not 测试台) for a stand or bench but 测试 for every "X Test" product and test system (HST 测试系统, never 试验系统), 校正 for unbalance correction (not 修正), 单平面/双平面 for planes, 马达 for hydraulic and 电机 for electric, 标定 for ECU/ADAS/turbo parameter setting and propulsion/powertrain end-of-line calibrations, 校准 for instruments.',
        'Convert English nominalisations and passives into Chinese verb phrases and active voice (new possibilities → 开辟新的可能), but an "opportunity to do X" keeps the opportunity as its head: "customers have new opportunities to collect data" is 客户有了采集数据的新机遇, never 客户可采集数据，获得新的机遇. A company name containing "powered by" (Current, powered by GE) stays in Latin. Avoid 被 unless the agent matters, never coin a noun absent from real Chinese industry writing, and never attach concrete adjectives to abstractions (可能性、机会).',
        'Consistency: one English term or label gets ONE Chinese rendering, identical on every surface (nav, H1, body, spec table, FAQ, card, footer, form, alt text, <title>, meta). Take the canonical form from the nav or footer and reuse it. Pick ONE rendering per term and per connector site-wide: 监测 (not 监控), 集成 (not 整合), 装配 (not 组装), 基地 (not 工厂) for a company site but 地点 for a UI or form field "Location", 表单 (not 表格), 与 (not 和) for "&" in nav labels. Treat OBD, NVH, HVAC, ADAS, NDT, BaaS, CaaS as a fixed set rendered identically everywhere; gloss an acronym as 中文全称（缩写） on first mention only, then hold one form. Translate every parallel SET as a set: Previous/Next on one noun axis (上一个／下一个), every option in one <select> in the same language, all siblings nominalised if one is, either all bullets and spec rows ending in 。 or none (headings and CTAs take none), every placeholder using ……, never ASCII "...". Two different English strings stay different: News 新闻 and Press 新闻稿.',
        'A spec-table or card label copies the English label\'s shape and adds nothing: End Drive (H2W) is 端部驱动（H2W）, not 端部驱动型（H2W）; U-axis control capability is U 轴控制能力, not 功能; "1 or 2 plane" is 单平面或双平面, never the clipped 单面; universal applicability is 通用性强; "Flows to 200 L/min" is 流量最高达 200 L/min. Keep the source\'s own head noun: an assembly is 组件／总成 (not 装配件), a component is 零部件 (not 工件). Recast a long English sentence into short Chinese clauses instead of tracking its syntax — do not chain 以…以…, do not end on 使…现代化 or 为…提供动力, and do not build a noun out of a purpose phrase: "Minimizes rework by catching system issues before assembly" is 在装配前发现系统问题，将返工降至最低, not 通过在装配前发现系统问题来最小化返工. Start on the circumstance and end on the assertion; do not calque maximize/minimize as a transitive verb (最大化设备价值 → 充分释放设备价值) and keep 性能 for machines only (business performance takes 业绩／效能／潜能); and prefer 了解 for Discover/See how, reserving 探索 for Explore.',
        'FIDELITY: never add, drop, strengthen or weaken a claim, modifier, number, qualifier or modality. "Addresses manufacturing process deficiencies" is 应对生产工艺缺陷, never 消除, but "eradicates all known weaknesses" IS 彻底消除 — render the verb the source wrote; a generic "under pressure" is 在压力之下, never narrowed to 工期紧迫. Superlatives survive, modals survive as 可／能／有助于, and no 率、度、倍 the English does not state may appear. Hold the narrow technical sense in thermal and rotating-machinery copy: "vapor" in a thermodynamic cycle is 蒸气, never 蒸汽 (steam); automotive "turbo" is always 涡轮增压器 while bare 涡轮 means turbine and belongs to aerospace and jet-engine contexts; in turbocharger contexts "core" is the cartridge 芯体 (涡轮增压器芯体), never 芯轴 and never 铁芯.',
        'Press releases and executive bios follow Chinese newswire convention, not English sentence order: the dateline lead names the company FIRST with the descriptor in apposition, one fixed string in every release and card (2026 年 3 月 31 日——Ascential Technologies，全球领先的自动化诊断、检测、装配与测试系统及服务提供商，业务覆盖广泛的……), a Division is 事业部 (never 部门) and the division name Test & Measurement Systems is translated, 测试与测量系统事业部 (this overrides the base division rule; only the lockup Ascential Test & Measurement stays Latin), a career line reads 此前曾任／离任前担任, never 最近担任, an award or programme name sits inside 中文引号（“集成化产品方案奖”）, and a quoted endorsement keeps the speaker\'s exact strength (拥有持续稳定的业绩记录, not 成绩卓著).',
        '应用领域 is the NAV CATEGORY label only; mid-sentence it renames the product. A tagline "for <X> applications" is always 适用于 X 领域 (for fluid power rotary motion applications = 适用于流体传动旋转运动领域), and "What applications is X used for?" is X 有哪些应用？, never 适用于哪些应用.',
        'Take a generic noun\'s shop-floor sense; never let a legal, medical, IT or office sense leak in: a valve "section" is 阀片 (never 条款), an EDT/EDM "generator" is 脉冲电源 (never 发电机), "injectors" are 充注头, "supervision" is 监视 (never 监督／监管), a counted "unit" is 台 (never 单位), a factory "cell" is 工位／生产单元 (never 单元格), a "line" is 生产线 (never 行), "machine down" is 设备停机 (never 宕机), roll "texturing" is 毛化 (never 纹理化／粗化), a support "case" is 工单 (never 案例). In a hydraulic, agricultural or aerospace parts list "motor" is 马达; only an electric motor is 电机. Likewise 数据 not 输入, 检出率 not 检测机会, 挂车 not 拖车, 任务关键型 not 关键任务型.',
        'Translate an event date-and-venue line whole, no English left: "May 20, 2025 · Stuttgart, Germany, Booth 1637" is 2025 年 5 月 20 日 · 德国斯图加特，1637 展位. Keep the spaces in 2025 年 5 月 20 日, expand every US state abbreviation (FL 佛罗里达州, PA 宾夕法尼亚州), use a place\'s established Chinese name, never a morpheme calque (Grapevine 格雷普韦恩, not 葡萄藤), render German "Messe X" as X 展览中心 (not 美塞), and keep the fair brand in Latin (Automechanika 2026).',
        'Copy spec-table figures, never re-key them — a European decimal comma becomes a point (0,75 kW → 0.75 kW), spacing around ／ between two figures is identical in every row of a table, the header "No." counts items (数量, never 编号), "phase" in a rating is 相数, never 相位, and 1ph／3 ph is 单相／三相, never 1 相／3 相.',
        'Cap any pre-nominal modifier at roughly 12 Chinese characters and never stack three 的 in one chain. Name the head noun FIRST and hang modifiers behind it instead of stacking every English post-modifier in front: "Engine cooling fan with motor balancing machine" is 带电机的发动机冷却风扇动平衡机. A product NAME ending "for <object>" is a compact compound with no 面向／用于 (Vertical Balancing Machines for Tools and Tool Holders = 刀具与刀柄立式动平衡机), identical in H1, alt text and FAQ; 面向……的 is for running prose only, and a long chain splits into a predicate clause (设备健康分析由打造这些测试系统的团队直接提供). Fold an English post-nominal example INSIDE the Chinese modifier (our brands, like Burke Porter → 包括 Burke Porter 在内的众多品牌), and give a bare gerund object its head noun (Elevating Support → 提升支持水平) without inventing a second clause — 提升支持，增进价值 adds a promise the source never made. Keep each asserted attribute as its own predicate (贴近客户、快速响应, never 就近响应); after 这一 use 该.',
        'Two taxonomy tags joined by an English comma take 、, not a dash: "Balancing, Transportation" is 动平衡、交通运输, never 动平衡——交通运输; a " - " title separator stays a spaced half-width hyphen (辅助阀测试 - Ascential Test & Measurement). In alt text translate every descriptive word: "on a transparent background" is 透明背景, "Person with long blonde hair" is 一位留着金色长发的人物, not 女性. Use 的／地／得 correctly and written positional words (上方的, never 上面的).',
        'Aerospace parts lists take aviation vocabulary: rotor blade 桨叶 (never 铲刀), engine oil 滑油 (never 机油), aircraft wheel 机轮 (never 车轮), preservation stand 封存台.',
        'A rename copula is neither a launch nor an ownership statement — "is now a product brand under X" is 现已成为 X 旗下的产品品牌, and 现已推出 is reserved for an actual NOW AVAILABLE product. Never add a head noun (平台／工具／导航／技术) to a heading or label that names only a capability: "Analytics that deliver timely insights" is 提供及时洞察的数据分析.',
		'Keep a neutral verb neutral and never rhetorically upgrade a flat one. "can significantly impact downtime, machine health and repairs" is 对停机、设备健康状况与维修产生显著影响 — never split it into 减少停机、改善健康、优化维修; "is a promise and our standard" is 既是承诺，也是我们的标准, not the 不仅……更是 escalation.',
		'Never downgrade a claim verb or swap a named capability for a neighbouring one. "predict failures" is 预测故障／预判故障 with the object kept, and 预警 is allowed only where the English says alert/warn/notify; 诊断 stays 诊断 (not 提示), 检测 stays 检测 (not 提醒). "collect, mine and measure data" is 采集、挖掘并测量数据 — rendering measure as 分析／衢量 silently replaces a named platform function with one already listed, and 测量 also matches the division name 测试与测量.',
		'Never change the noun a statistic counts, and give every counter its measure word. Countries stays 国家 (not 市场), people 人才／人员 (not 团队), locations 基地 (not 市场) — buyers put these numbers in comparison spreadsheets. Counter labels are numerals at runtime even though the HTML shows 0, so write 个国家, 名专业人才, 个全球基地, never the bare noun; "home countries" becomes the predicate 个国家设有本土团队, "years of innovation" is 年创新历程 (never bare 年创新), "projects and counting" is 个项目，且数量仍在不断增加.',
		'Keep every modifier and every relation the English states. Trailing purpose phrases survive ("for their consumers" = 为其消费者); an adverbial of duration attaches to the verb the English attaches it to ("Watch how we integrate X ... in a few minutes" is 用几分钟时间，观看我们如何将…集成…, never 观看我们如何在几分钟内将…, which claims the integration takes minutes); and the agent of a "for/from" noun phrase survives ("support requests for Bauer customers and other partners" means requests FROM them: Bauer 客户及其他合作伙伴提交的支持请求, not 对……的支持请求).',
		'Every Chinese verb needs its object, and every verb-object pair must be one that occurs in real Chinese industry writing. "allowing us to adapt swiftly" is 使我们能够迅速应变, never the objectless 迅速适应 — 适应、响应、提升、改善、满足 all require a stated object even where English drops it, and an English prepositional tail needs its own clause. Use 应对／迎接挑战 (never 解决挑战), 解决难题, 满足需求, 积累经验, 开展检测, 优化流程／配置 (never 优化需求), 缩短处理时间 (never 改善…时间), 汇聚人才／资源 (never 汇聚头脑), 交付智能系统并为其提供支持 for "deliver and support systems" (支持 + a product object reads as "endorse"); do not coordinate unlike categories under one verb just because English does; and a Chinese machine 做 a motion, it does not 执行 one.',
		'Never repeat the same morpheme inside one clause or label, and break a collision by changing the HEAD NOUN rather than the register. 无损检测 already IS non-destructive testing, so "NDT inspection" is 无损检测（NDT）, never 无损检测（NDT）检测; "Support & consulting sales inquiry" is 支持与咨询业务销售咨询, with the 销售咨询 suffix byte-identical across every sibling.',
		'Delete the second marker and the perfective 了 when the clause does not need them: 在故障发生前预警, never 在故障发生前提前预警 (same for 提前预先、事先预判、再次重复); "streamlines validation, improves throughput" is 简化验证流程、提高吞吐量, not 简化了…、提高了…, which reports a completed past event instead of a standing capability.',
		'Never open a Chinese sentence with a bare 或 copied from an English "Or ..." sentence — use 或者，… or fold the clause into the preceding sentence — and never open with a subjectless participial clause: "In a strategic move reflecting its commitment to X, Y announced…" is 作为一项战略举措，Y 宣布……，彰显其……的一贯承诺。 Split it; never stack the whole frame in front of 举措／方案／计划, and never turn it into a purpose clause with 为体现……, which converts substance into image management.',
		'Rewrite English word order into Chinese shape. Questions and headings go topic-comment: "How can we help you today?" is 今天我们能为您提供什么帮助？, "What\'s new at X?" is the noun phrase X 最新动态, "Searching <site>" labels a scope (在 <site> 中搜索, not 正在搜索). Job titles are strictly left-branching, unit first, and a business segment takes 业务 so it cannot read as a trade or a technology: "CTO of Transportation" is 交通运输业务首席技术官, "Vice President of Technology, Aerospace & Industrials" is 航空航天与工业业务技术副总裁 (never 部门); a place name stays a proper noun (Three Rivers 基地总经理). Appointment headlines: Hires X as = 聘任 X 为, Promotes X to = 擢升 X 为 (晋升 is intransitive), Welcomes X as = 迎来 X 出任. Degrees rebuild as 在<机构>取得<专业><学位> with established names (Master of Science in X = X 理学硕士), and a person takes a full Latin name on first mention then the established transliteration — never a bare Latin surname as the subject of a Chinese sentence.',
		'A one-word English nav category is often a clipped technical compound — expand it to the full Chinese industry term, and keep wayfinding labels plain and literal: "Power" in a driveline menu is 动力总成, "Vision" in an inspection menu is 机器视觉, "Locations" is 全球基地 (never 全球布局). When "machine" modifies data or analytics, translate the OBJECT (设备健康分析, never 机器分析).',
		'Read service-offer wording against the commercial model. "Contract balancing as-a-service" is 委托动平衡即服务（BaaS）, because 合同 is the paper contract and 合同动平衡 parses as "balancing of a contract", while unqualified "balancing-as-a-service" stays 动平衡即服务. "Gauging" in a capability list is dimensional gauging, 尺寸检测, never 测量. "Available X" in a menu of purchasable options goes predicate-final: 多种服务级别协议可选, not 可选服务级别协议 (readable as "the SLA is optional") and never 可用, which misparses as an availability (uptime) SLA.',
		'Keep the engineering colour of a verb used by an engineering company, and use a neutral adverb for corporate capability. "we engineer new possibilities" is 我们以工程之力开创新的可能, never bare 开创／打造; "from the team that builds the test systems" is 由打造这些测试系统的团队直接提供, never 亲自提供, and never 倾情、用心、贴心 in B2B equipment copy. Never translate a hortative CTA with 让我们 plus a verb — no Chinese CTA uses that calque: "Let\'s talk" is 洽谈合作, "Let\'s get started" is 立即开始, "Join us" is 加入我们, and if a sibling already renders 联系我们 for "Contact us", pick the other option so two different English CTAs stay distinct.',
		'Form microcopy is written as native Chinese UI, not as translated English sentences. A <select> placeholder "Select an option" is 请选择 (never 选择一个选项); "Any error codes from the system you can share?" is 可否提供系统报出的错误代码？; "select from the forms below" keeps the choosing, 从下方选择相应表单填写, never 填写下方表单. In a chat or contact widget "message" is 消息, never 信息, and every input placeholder takes 请 plus a verb (请输入您的姓名), except a search box: 搜索产品……. A lead-in before an inline phone number ends on 致电: "You can phone us for sales assistance at" is 如需销售协助，请致电, never 您可致电我们，电话：.',
		'Translate EVERY string a cookie/consent component prints: table headers (名称／域名／有效期), 项 Cookie, every aria-label (Cookie consent → Cookie 同意设置), durations in Chinese units (2 年, 30 分钟, session = 会话期间). Controls go verb-first ("Google Analytics Opt Out" = 退出 Google Analytics 跟踪, "Manage cookie preferences" = 管理 Cookie 偏好设置), never ending on 选择退出, and "Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information" stays imperative: 请勿出售或分享我的个人信息.',
		'aria-label navigation landmarks name the region, not the English adjective: "Primary" is 主导航, "Mobile primary" is 移动端主导航 — never 主要, never 移动端优先 (the mobile-first design philosophy). Only an adjective landmark gains 导航; a noun label keeps its own noun (Sidebar = 侧边栏, never 侧边栏导航).',
		'Named offerings are brands even when every word looks translatable. If a phrase is a product or service name in a nav, footer product column or menu card (ADAS Garage, XL Machine, Lismar, Titan, WinterPark, Ascential Care), keep the WHOLE name in Latin script. Never half-translate a brand in one place and keep it in another on the same page, never attach ™ to a translated phrase, and when a label wraps a brand in <span class="tmm-brand-word">, ONLY the brand belongs inside that span.',
		'Translate an English abbreviation for a generic role, activity or object — Chinese readers mis-expand it (SME reads as 中小企业, PM as 项目经理): SME is 领域专家, PM (maintenance) 预防性维护, MUT 被测电机, DUT 被测件, BEMF 反电动势 (this overrides the base rule on bare acronyms). Keep Latin only for acronyms Chinese engineers write in Latin (NVH, ADAS, CAN, UDS, TCP, ERP, PLC). A lowercase descriptive feature name is copy, not a brand: "First alert monitoring system" is 早期预警监测系统.',
		'Place Chinese frames where Chinese grammar puts them. 作为……的一部分 opens the sentence before its subject (作为端到端支持服务的一部分，我们……, never 我们作为……的一部分); "is integral to X" makes the part the subject (工作油口通常集成于 HST 内部，其流量无法测量); "sizes range from X to Y" is 规格从 X 到 Y 不等, never 覆盖从面向…用…的系统; a qualifier on the last list item (as required, if equipped) stays on that item (…以及按需测试壳体泄油流量和清洁度), never fronted where it governs the whole list; "regardless of location" attaches to the benefit it conditions. A subject "The system" is 该系统, because bare 系统 before a verb fuses into the noun 系统测试 (该系统用于测试装配正确性、机械效率…). "At CIMAT, we offer" makes the company the subject (CIMAT 提供), and after a company-name subject "our" is 其／自身, never 我们的.',
		'Drop English service-marketing calques: "customers can expect X" is 客户可获得／均能享有 X (never 可期待), "at every step of their journey" is 在每个环节 (never 旅程), "actionable information" is 可指导行动的信息 (never 可付诸行动的), "now united under one roof" is 现已整合为一体 (never 同一屋檐之下), a list closing "and beyond"/"and more" ends on 等 (泄漏检测等, never ，以及更多), and a relative clause keeps its causal link: "experiences that drive value" is 服务体验，从而创造……价值.',
		'In a service-plan or price matrix a short cell is a value of its row label, and every repeated label is character-identical in each table: a shipping priority "Next" is 下一班次 and "Next day" 次日 (never the pager 下一个), a "Preferred" tier is 优惠／优惠费率 (never 优选), labor and labour are both 人工, training "update & refresh" is 更新与巩固. A frequency tier cell is 年度／半年度 (Semi-annual (update & refresh) = 半年度（更新与巩固）), an included visit is 含每年／每半年一次上门服务 (never 出行), and a clipped label reuses the noun of its full row name (Review under Training review = 回顾, never 评审). Every cell gets a translation, however short.',
		'Use Simplified characters (简体), never Traditional, and full-width punctuation inside every Chinese sentence: ，。、；：？！, curly quotes “ ” and （） — even when the English source shows ASCII " \' ( ). Half-width characters appear only inside an untranslated Latin run. Use full-width ／ for every slash inside Chinese copy (轻微磨损／损伤) and 《》 for a document title before 白皮书. A colon title embedded in a sentence puts its subtitle in （）: 如需就驱动电机试验台（电机精密测试）获取定制报价, never a mid-sentence ：.',
		'Insert a single half-width space only where real Latin text or digits sit next to Chinese (使用 API 接口) — never around an inline <span> or <a> inside a Chinese sentence (将一切<span>融为一体</span>) and never between two Chinese characters.',
		'Numbers use Western digits with a comma thousands separator exactly as the source writes them (15,000 r/min, never 15 000), currency 1,500 元, dates 2026 年 9 月 22 日, 24-hour time (14:30).',
	),
